body:
No-override uniqueness across the merged library: the external and local layers merge with no precedence, so a name carried in two places is a validation error rather than an override. The merged registry keys templates by name in a single template namespace shared by slides and sections, so slide and section names are unique together across both layers — a local slide named like an external section (or vice versa) is a duplicate. Theme names form a separate namespace, and `media/` files are keyed by their own path. A duplicate is a templates error naming the duplicated name and both paths (the file or directory that carries it in each layer), reported before any deck is served. Within one layer the same single-namespace uniqueness holds across `slides/` and `sections/` (templates-dir-layout).

AC:
- an external slide named `content` and a local slide named `content` is a templates error naming `content` and both paths;
- an external and a local section named `columns` is a templates error naming `columns` and both paths;
- a local slide named `x` and an external section named `x` (or an external slide named `x` and a local section named `x`) is a templates error naming `x` and both paths;
- an external and a local theme named `default` is a templates error naming `default` and both paths;
- an external and a local `media/` path naming the same file is a templates error naming the path and both roots;
- two layers with disjoint slide, section, theme and media names merge and load cleanly.
